quiet.md #16: Windows clipboard: PNG for bitmaps, copied files as images

Upstream now reads text, one image (CF_DIB included) and copied files in one
pass. On top of that: a bitmap tool may list CF_DIB before its PNG, so prefer
the PNG and otherwise turn the bitmap into a PNG (the document stores it; a
BMP is large). Upstream's DIB conversion adds the 12 bytes of BI_BITFIELDS
masks for V4/V5 headers too, which hold them inside the header, and shifts
the picture: use our conversion. Copied files that are all images (Explorer)
paste as those images; other copied files paste as their paths, one per
line, when there is no text.

